If *C* measures *D, A* also measures *B.* But *A* does not measure *B,* therefore neither does *C* measure *D.* [!just VIII.14]

* * *

Next, let *C* not measure *D.*

I say that neither does *A* measure *B.*

If *A* measures *B,* then *C* also measures *D.* But *C* does not measure *D,* therefore neither does *A* measure *B.* [!just VIII.14]

Therefore, *if a square does not measure a square, then neither does the side measure the side; and, if the side does not measure the side, then neither does the square measure the square.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide: This is simply the contrapositive of @VIII.14. It is unclear why papyrus was wasted to state and prove it.
